{"id":"5176831d-ac38-46ee-9cb9-bc3eaa6b8cb1","title":"12SEN_Cycle2","fetched":"2026-10-23T23:58:44.961Z","questions":[{"id":"1fc90651-ad83-4c0a-8647-23732102acff","title":"Privacy By Design (SA, TKS 2025)","isPublished":true,"publishDate":"2025-07-21T05:16:34.012Z","syllabusId":"d1a54432-597e-4e3c-a5c6-ad7a134726e4","stimulusContentItemCollection":{"id":"aedc79f3-5d72-450a-b2a1-87611074819c","items":[{"id":"41a08ca0-0497-4505-a4cf-8045a984eaa4","updatedDate":"2025-07-01T23:20:22.248Z","files":null,"type":"RICH_TEXT","text":"<p>An e-commerce platform is being developed. During planning, the team performs a privacy impact assessment and decides to minimise customer data collection, avoid storing payment details, and enable encrypted guest checkout.</p>"}],"itemIdOrder":["41a08ca0-0497-4505-a4cf-8045a984eaa4"]},"publisher":null,"dynamicFields":null,"copyrightText":"TKS 2025","visibility":"PRIVATE","school":{"id":"7572b03a-1507-4309-950e-2a286bdcf0a4","name":"The King's School, Parramatta"},"systemId":null,"system":null,"isPublisherLocked":false,"parts":[{"id":"5c2852b8-d30a-45e4-bfc5-990bc0a114d6","displayIndex":0,"title":"Part A","metadata":{"id":"17374994-b12a-42be-9c3e-35884169b908","mark":3,"syllabus":{"id":"d1a54432-597e-4e3c-a5c6-ad7a134726e4","title":"Software Engineering","description":"Software Engineering Stage 6 Syllabus 2022","gradeFrom":12,"gradeTo":12,"coverageLabel":null,"curriculumCode":null,"curriculumVersion":null,"gradingScaleName":null,"publishedYear":null,"publishedDate":null},"band":null,"outcomeIds":["858fde69-da06-440b-8093-01c934aebcfa","d37b0608-71dc-40b5-9bdd-791cd53903ee","62083f53-20d4-4148-9a06-ef580b3b6dd0"],"topicIds":["a45d4626-6ce7-44bc-b6a2-d0fcaeea9412"],"subtopicIds":["07c5c11b-d8f6-401d-ac93-0e1b7ca1a1d1"],"subtopicItemIds":["8396603f-df7e-4c16-a182-9e769e71d3f1"],"bandIds":["266e22f1-3f8a-4fbd-95bd-e7a6221d1c65","b87d71ee-5ae9-43f7-a1f5-feec3f1db295"]},"content":{"id":"a248b750-bcb4-4c7b-95bc-679775aae227","contentItemCollection":{"id":"e2d4ceaf-6643-4cb8-a60d-c83ab10076ac","items":[{"id":"e996591f-cd00-480d-aca2-40e72343357d","updatedDate":"2025-07-01T23:20:28.807Z","files":null,"type":"RICH_TEXT","text":"<p>Explain how the team&rsquo;s actions demonstrate the <em data-start=\"333\" data-end=\"352\">Privacy by Design</em> approach</p>"}],"itemIdOrder":["e996591f-cd00-480d-aca2-40e72343357d"]},"contentItemMetadata":null},"answer":{"id":"0bb091b9-31ae-4785-98b5-72f074ff51a8","parameters":{"version":0,"type":"SHORT","extendedView":true,"settings":{"version":0,"wordLimit":false,"wordCount":null,"exactValue":false,"richText":true,"imageUpload":false,"equationEditor":false,"calculatorInterface":false},"correctValues":null},"files":null},"markingCriteriaContentItem":{"id":"8b2ae012-7430-4f23-bd54-e08db127b57d","updatedDate":"2025-07-01T23:20:51.517Z","files":null,"type":"MARKING_CRITERIA","criteria":[{"criterion":"<p>Demonstrates a thorough understanding of the Privacy by Design approach; clearly connects scenario elements to key principles</p>","point":"<p>3</p>"},{"criterion":"<p>Shows sound understanding; identifies at least two principles with relevant explanation.</p>","point":"<p>2</p>"},{"criterion":"<p>Identifies one relevant principle with some basic explanation.</p>","point":"<p>1</p>"}]},"markingRubricContentItem":null,"markingGuidanceContentItem":null,"sampleAnswerContentItem":{"id":"9308d1a0-3579-48d6-8cae-844cbebd2f61","updatedDate":"2025-07-01T23:21:00.191Z","files":null,"type":"RICH_TEXT","text":"<p>The team&rsquo;s actions reflect several key principles of Privacy by Design. Conducting a privacy impact assessment early shows a <em data-start=\"1285\" data-end=\"1296\">proactive</em> approach by identifying potential risks before launch. Choosing not to store payment details and enabling encrypted guest checkout are examples of <em data-start=\"1444\" data-end=\"1479\">embedding privacy into the design</em>, ensuring secure and minimal data handling from the outset. Limiting the amount of data collected respects users' privacy by reducing exposure risk and enhancing user trust. Together, these practices show a comprehensive application of the Privacy by Design framework.</p>"}}]},{"id":"913e078b-dda4-47a1-8f44-98b8fcc600b2","title":"Security By Design (SA, TKS 2025)","isPublished":true,"publishDate":"2025-06-29T09:53:32.379Z","syllabusId":"d1a54432-597e-4e3c-a5c6-ad7a134726e4","stimulusContentItemCollection":null,"publisher":null,"dynamicFields":null,"copyrightText":"TKS 2025","visibility":"PRIVATE","school":{"id":"7572b03a-1507-4309-950e-2a286bdcf0a4","name":"The King's School, Parramatta"},"systemId":null,"system":null,"isPublisherLocked":false,"parts":[{"id":"76fe8bf1-73ae-448b-a204-e217010af8c4","displayIndex":0,"title":"Part 1","metadata":{"id":"c4958657-47a0-445e-aca5-0264c17db710","mark":4,"syllabus":{"id":"d1a54432-597e-4e3c-a5c6-ad7a134726e4","title":"Software Engineering","description":"Software Engineering Stage 6 Syllabus 2022","gradeFrom":12,"gradeTo":12,"coverageLabel":null,"curriculumCode":null,"curriculumVersion":null,"gradingScaleName":null,"publishedYear":null,"publishedDate":null},"band":null,"outcomeIds":["d37b0608-71dc-40b5-9bdd-791cd53903ee","62083f53-20d4-4148-9a06-ef580b3b6dd0","858fde69-da06-440b-8093-01c934aebcfa"],"topicIds":["a45d4626-6ce7-44bc-b6a2-d0fcaeea9412"],"subtopicIds":["07c5c11b-d8f6-401d-ac93-0e1b7ca1a1d1"],"subtopicItemIds":["737b0a0e-2ec2-4ea4-b8dc-4d77fe070539"],"bandIds":["266e22f1-3f8a-4fbd-95bd-e7a6221d1c65","b87d71ee-5ae9-43f7-a1f5-feec3f1db295"]},"content":{"id":"7be8480e-9ad4-4805-af56-2f5aee816ef7","contentItemCollection":{"id":"ca6112e4-9c70-4088-80dd-c724881f28dd","items":[{"id":"58d88dea-2c1d-4701-b038-21f66f5fd7a3","updatedDate":"2025-06-26T00:12:03.928Z","files":null,"type":"RICH_TEXT","text":"<p>A company is developing a cloud-based document sharing platform.</p>\n<p>Describe how both cryptography and sandboxing can work together to enhance the platform&rsquo;s security.</p>"}],"itemIdOrder":["58d88dea-2c1d-4701-b038-21f66f5fd7a3"]},"contentItemMetadata":null},"answer":{"id":"477e7bf4-1a51-40e7-8cd2-a07f7c7baf1f","parameters":{"version":0,"type":"SHORT","extendedView":true,"settings":{"version":0,"wordLimit":false,"wordCount":null,"exactValue":false,"richText":true,"imageUpload":false,"equationEditor":false,"calculatorInterface":false},"correctValues":null},"files":null},"markingCriteriaContentItem":{"id":"57d1263c-54cf-482e-91ce-c1909e2d6bba","updatedDate":"2025-06-26T00:13:38.981Z","files":null,"type":"MARKING_CRITERIA","criteria":[{"criterion":"<p>Explains clearly how both cryptography and sandboxing improve security, with relevant details and examples.</p>","point":"<p>4</p>"},{"criterion":"<p>Outlines the contributions of both cryptography and sandboxing with some detail.</p>","point":"<p>3</p>"},{"criterion":"<p>Describes one technique clearly and mentions the other.</p>","point":"<p>2</p>"},{"criterion":"<p>Shows some understanding of either cryptography or sandboxing.</p>","point":"<p>1</p>"}]},"markingRubricContentItem":null,"markingGuidanceContentItem":null,"sampleAnswerContentItem":{"id":"2d4d8ee0-9649-4fb4-a9d1-d8283248947f","updatedDate":"2025-06-26T00:11:39.072Z","files":null,"type":"RICH_TEXT","text":"<p>Cryptography supports authentication by verifying the identities of users or devices through techniques like digital signatures and certificates. These methods use encrypted keys that prove a user is who they claim to be, preventing unauthorised access. By ensuring only authorised parties can access the software, cryptography strengthens security and helps protect sensitive information from attackers.</p>"}}]},{"id":"a884290e-b222-480f-b814-b8019e70de2a","title":"Defensive Data (SA, TKS 2025)","isPublished":true,"publishDate":"2025-09-15T04:28:01.143Z","syllabusId":"d1a54432-597e-4e3c-a5c6-ad7a134726e4","stimulusContentItemCollection":null,"publisher":null,"dynamicFields":null,"copyrightText":"TKS 2025","visibility":"PRIVATE","school":{"id":"7572b03a-1507-4309-950e-2a286bdcf0a4","name":"The King's School, Parramatta"},"systemId":null,"system":null,"isPublisherLocked":false,"parts":[{"id":"3e4b8ee7-7b55-4c77-b1af-bb952cdd4241","displayIndex":0,"title":"Part A","metadata":{"id":"31276224-276b-4e21-b2b8-96d62a582456","mark":3,"syllabus":{"id":"d1a54432-597e-4e3c-a5c6-ad7a134726e4","title":"Software Engineering","description":"Software Engineering Stage 6 Syllabus 2022","gradeFrom":12,"gradeTo":12,"coverageLabel":null,"curriculumCode":null,"curriculumVersion":null,"gradingScaleName":null,"publishedYear":null,"publishedDate":null},"band":null,"outcomeIds":["d37b0608-71dc-40b5-9bdd-791cd53903ee","858fde69-da06-440b-8093-01c934aebcfa"],"topicIds":["a45d4626-6ce7-44bc-b6a2-d0fcaeea9412"],"subtopicIds":["07c5c11b-d8f6-401d-ac93-0e1b7ca1a1d1"],"subtopicItemIds":["1d656214-cb39-4959-8632-2a94338572d8"],"bandIds":["266e22f1-3f8a-4fbd-95bd-e7a6221d1c65","b87d71ee-5ae9-43f7-a1f5-feec3f1db295"]},"content":{"id":"07a0f7d0-1135-43ad-8d3b-adb6547c0700","contentItemCollection":{"id":"44645941-f1c0-437a-9b05-932e7b20e49e","items":[{"id":"c548a836-5f9b-452b-b1d3-85c0269628c4","updatedDate":"2025-07-02T00:09:49.442Z","files":null,"type":"RICH_TEXT","text":"<p>Describe one difference between client-side and server-side input validation, and explain why both are important in a secure application</p>"}],"itemIdOrder":["c548a836-5f9b-452b-b1d3-85c0269628c4"]},"contentItemMetadata":null},"answer":{"id":"a5e0ea0c-e54a-41f9-a9d9-454e9597b846","parameters":{"version":0,"type":"SHORT","extendedView":true,"settings":{"version":0,"wordLimit":false,"wordCount":null,"exactValue":false,"richText":true,"imageUpload":false,"equationEditor":false,"calculatorInterface":false},"correctValues":null},"files":null},"markingCriteriaContentItem":{"id":"c19ac46c-2ebd-4182-a55a-ef2c06dec5c4","updatedDate":"2025-07-02T00:10:13.720Z","files":null,"type":"MARKING_CRITERIA","criteria":[{"criterion":"<p>Clearly describes the difference and explains the importance of using both client- and server-side validation in a secure context</p>","point":"<p>3</p>"},{"criterion":"<p>Describes the difference and gives a sound explanation of one reason why both are used.</p>","point":"<p>2</p>"},{"criterion":"<p>Identifies a basic difference but explanation is unclear or incomplete.</p>","point":"<p>1</p>"}]},"markingRubricContentItem":null,"markingGuidanceContentItem":null,"sampleAnswerContentItem":{"id":"ac3f8e89-dca1-43f2-8048-6dc5c855e73a","updatedDate":"2025-07-02T00:10:00.612Z","files":null,"type":"RICH_TEXT","text":"<p>Client-side validation is performed in the user&rsquo;s browser before the data is sent to the server, while server-side validation happens after the data reaches the server. Client-side checks improve the user experience by providing quick feedback, but they can be bypassed by attackers. Server-side validation is more secure because it ensures all data is properly checked before it is processed or stored. Using both together ensures better usability and strong protection against invalid or malicious input</p>"}}]}],"answers":[{"partId":"5c2852b8-d30a-45e4-bfc5-990bc0a114d6","studentId":"0071efd7-8807-43a2-96e7-9085b48c8632","examAnswerSheetItem":null,"mark":null,"markingSessionMarkingItemList":[]},{"partId":"76fe8bf1-73ae-448b-a204-e217010af8c4","studentId":"0071efd7-8807-43a2-96e7-9085b48c8632","examAnswerSheetItem":null,"mark":null,"markingSessionMarkingItemList":[]},{"partId":"3e4b8ee7-7b55-4c77-b1af-bb952cdd4241","studentId":"0071efd7-8807-43a2-96e7-9085b48c8632","examAnswerSheetItem":null,"mark":null,"markingSessionMarkingItemList":[]}],"state":{"isFinished":true,"dynamicFieldSeed":null,"markerUserList":[{"id":"4e096daa-d1c7-47e9-9c7b-c1adaf476532","firstName":"TKS","lastName":"CST"}],"examTitle":"12SEN_Cycle2"}}